## What shipped

The B3 registration flow already had a working PaymentSheet path for the
`registration` kind. D2 generalizes it and wires the two missing kinds
(`transportation`, `priceItem`), mirroring iOS.

- **Reusable CTA** (`ui/payments/CzPaymentButton` + `PaymentButtonViewModel`):
  one inline "pay this fee" button mirroring the iOS `PaymentButton`. Runs the
  full flow — `POST /payments/intent` → present native PaymentSheet → on
  completion `POST /payments/confirm` → `onPaid`. Renders a "no payment due" /
  "payment exempt" badge when the request carries no amount. Scoped per item via
  `hiltViewModel(key = …)` so many instances coexist in one list. The Stripe
  secret never leaves the backend; the client only holds the publishable key +
  ephemeral secret returned by the intent call.
- **Transportation fare CTA** (`ui/transportation`): per-booking CTA beneath
  each `BusTicketCard` on the passenger tickets screen — `kind = transportation`,
  `referenceID = booking.id`, amount/currency from the resolved
  `CampingTransportationOption`. Only the actionable unpaid case shows the CTA
  (paid/waived stay on the header status pill). `TransportationViewModel.reloadTickets()`
  silently re-pulls bookings after the backend flips `paymentStatus`.
- **"Fees & Payments" hub** (`ui/camping/pricing/CampingPricingScreen` +
  `CampingPricingViewModel`): mirrors iOS `CampingPricingView` and folds in any
  still-unpaid registration fees. Price-item card supports one-off card,
  3-payment installment (first slice now), and IBAN bank-transfer copy. The
  camp-detail "Fees & Payments" entry now routes here, gated on
  `hasPendingRegistrationPayment || hasPayablePriceItems`.
- **Model**: `CampingPriceItemPayments.kt` ports the iOS price-item helpers
  (`installmentAmountCents`, `resolvedCurrency`, `offersCardOneTime/Installments/BankTransfer`).
- **i18n**: new payment/fees strings added to EN, PT-BR, FR.

## Data contract

- Amount always integer cents; `PaymentRequest.normalizedCurrency` lowercases
  the API currency (`eur`); price items keep uppercase ISO for display.
- `referenceID` = attendee id (registration), booking id (transportation),
  price-item id (priceItem). Client never writes `registrationStatus` /
  `paymentStatus`; the backend settles them on confirm.

## Deferred (iOS-richer, not in the Android contract)

- PDF invoice receipts (`PaymentInvoicePDFView`) and the payment-proof/history
